<code>assert (index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \result.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the `set` method: it returns the element previously at the given position. The comment says: if the index is valid, the returned value equals the element that was at that position before the update.

A valid index is `0 <= index < size` (the size before the operation), and `\result` should equal the element that was there before, which is `\old(this.get(index))`.

<code>assert (0 <= index && index < \old(this.size())) => \result.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>
--------------------
